@startuml
title CyberRecon — Self-Destruct Sequence (v3.5)

actor Operator
participant "Dashboard" as DB
participant "C2 Server" as C2
participant "Victim Client" as VC
participant "Windows Registry" as REG
participant "Filesystem" as FS

Operator -> DB : Click Self Destruct
DB -> C2 : POST /command/<id> (session + operator token)
C2 -> C2 : Queue command
C2 --> DB : 200 OK

VC -> C2 : GET /qr/<id> (X-Victim-Key)
C2 --> VC : QR PNG (AES-encrypted)
VC -> VC : Decode to dispatch handler

VC -> REG : Delete HKCU Run WindowsSecurityUpdate
VC -> REG : Delete HKCU Software CyberRecon
VC -> REG : Clear RunMRU and RecentDocs
VC -> FS  : Delete temp scripts, chrome profiles, sandbox contents
VC -> C2  : POST /self_destruct_notify/<id>
C2 -> C2  : Delete victims_state.json entry
C2 --> VC : 200 wiped

VC -> FS  : Write temp self-destruct batch
VC -> FS  : Spawn detached cmd.exe
VC --> VC : os._exit(0)

note over FS
  Detached batch waits 3s then:
   - del /f /q payload.exe
   - del /f /q batch
end note

@enduml